    <p class="fs-caption fs-stack" id="attn-notes"><span data-note="camera" data-on>Scores recorded October 17, 13:51, one a second (the agent samples twice a second), replayed through the repo's own rule. The person is a separate, cleaner take from October 19, traced as outlines of the body and the raised arm, and two eye points; no image is kept. The take plays at real speed and the scores are lined up with its raises; where the scores run faster, the axis says so. Drag across the rows, and drag the bars.</span><span data-note="point">An illustration: the pointer is generated, not recorded, from a model calibrated on how 120 people moved a mouse in the SapiMouse dataset (a fast curved push that lands a little short, then a correction or two). The 0.61 is a real confidence from October 17. Drag across the rows to scrub.</span></p>
